# Keeps the Docker build context small and, just as importantly, makes a local
# `docker build` see the SAME tree Render does. Render builds from a clean git
# clone, so anything .gitignore hides is already absent there; mirroring those
# entries here stops a local build from silently succeeding on files that will
# not exist in CI.
#
# Unpruned the context is ~460 MB, nearly all of it irrelevant to a web build:
#   recapture-api 179M · build 96M · .dart_tool 60M · recapture 55M
#   .git 34M · android 32M
# Pruned it is a few MB, which is uploaded to the daemon on every single build.

# ── Never ships, and would defeat the layer cache ────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Regenerated inside the image by `flutter pub get` / `flutter build web`.
# Copying a host .dart_tool in would overwrite the package_config.json the
# builder just produced, with paths that do not exist in the container.
.dart_tool
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
build/
coverage/

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Also .gitignore'd. The Dockerfile regenerates these from ARG API_BASE_URL;
# excluding them here guarantees a stray local .env can never be baked into a
# published image, where it would be world-readable at /assets/.env.
.env
.env.dev
.env.staging
.env.prod

# ── Other platforms — a web build needs none of them ─────────────────────────
android/
ios/
macos/
linux/
windows/
fastlane/
Gemfile
Gemfile.lock

# ── Not part of this Flutter app ─────────────────────────────────────────────
recapture-api/
recapture/
maya-viewer/
node_modules/
docker-compose.yml

# ── Dev-only ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
test/
docs/
DOC/
*.md
*.txt
*.iml
.vscode/
.idea/
Makefile
